From cc3ae0f2f3e23ec904cf41e7d9bdc630c303411c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wmehanna <wassimmehanna@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:43:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vmapple): bring the guest clock back in line after a
 restore

- Count the generic timer at exactly CNTFRQ (x-exact-cntfrq=off keeps
  the old way, an older stream keeps counting the old way). The old
  divisor made a 24 MHz guest run 1.6 percent fast.
- sync-clock-on-load (opt in): the wall time of the save goes into the
  stream and the first run after a load moves the VM clock forward by
  the host time since then. The advance is counted from the stop, not
  from the device state write, which runs after the RAM of a
  mapped-ram save is written.
- cntfrq-exact system test.
---
